# Random modules as in random-existentials.test, with an existentially
# typed constructor too, built with 'new shown'(...) and taken apart by a
# function, and rarely built without new, which is a type error
# (generate-random-programs.py --existential-constructors).
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-random-programs.py --existential-constructors --seed 3 --count 60 %t
# RUN: %compare-types --allow-errors %t/*.m
